// 인용은 notes/web/<id>.txt 에 글자 그대로 있다(공백 차이 제외). 그림 글자는 notes/figures.md 에 있고 source 는 그 그림이 실린 w1 이다.
{"id": "e1", "source": "w1", "locator": "§intro bullets", "quote": "A structured, auditable knowledge architecture separates what the agent knows from how it reasons.", "why": "Meta 의 두 층 중 첫째"}
{"id": "e2", "source": "w1", "locator": "§intro bullets", "quote": "A self-improvement loop then compiles expert feedback into verified, regression-tested updates without model retraining.", "why": "Meta 의 두 층 중 둘째, 재학습 없음"}
{"id": "e3", "source": "w1", "locator": "§intro bullets", "quote": "the pattern is designed to generalize to other domains governed by retrievable text rather than model weights", "why": "일반화 조건: 가중치가 아니라 텍스트로 통제되는 영역"}
{"id": "e4", "source": "w1", "locator": "§intro", "quote": "In compliance domains, for example, the same types of questions can arise across hundreds of product reviews, expert assessments take days of manual research, and inconsistency between assessments creates real organizational risk.", "why": "problem: 같은 질문 반복, 며칠, 불일치"}
{"id": "e5", "source": "w1", "locator": "§The Architecture at a Glance", "quote": "it will not be able to distinguish between what an organization could do (a summary of general information) and what it should consider doing (based on historic positions, company direction, business context, etc.)", "why": "범용 LLM 의 한계: could vs should"}
{"id": "e6", "source": "w1", "locator": "§The Architecture at a Glance", "quote": "The knowledge system’s file structure makes automated editing possible. The reasoning layer’s explicit procedures make failure attribution tractable. The evaluation framework gates every change.", "why": "네 층의 상호 의존"}
{"id": "e7", "source": "w1", "locator": "§The Architecture at a Glance", "quote": "Remove any one layer and the others degrade.", "why": "층 하나를 빼면 나머지가 약해진다"}
{"id": "e8", "source": "w1", "locator": "§Building the Organizational Second Brain", "quote": "An agent that retrieves document chunks at inference time has to re-derive that reasoning from raw sources on every run, which is slow, error-prone, and inconsistent.", "why": "chunk RAG 의 문제 정의"}
{"id": "e9", "source": "w1", "locator": "§Building the Organizational Second Brain", "quote": "A long-running offline process reasons through source documents and distills them into structured knowledge files", "why": "오프라인 증류"}
{"id": "e10", "source": "w1", "locator": "§Building the Organizational Second Brain", "quote": "Andrej Karpathy’s LLM Wiki structures agent knowledge as a navigable graph of files, and Google’s Open Knowledge Format standardizes this for cross-agent interoperability.", "why": "Meta 가 스스로 대는 계보"}
{"id": "e11", "source": "w1", "locator": "§Building the Organizational Second Brain", "quote": "We extended these principles into a system where citation fidelity and institutional consistency are non-negotiable, organizing 200+ files into a strict taxonomy:", "why": "200+ files 숫자"}
{"id": "e12", "source": "w1", "locator": "§Building the Organizational Second Brain", "quote": "Position files capture authoritative organizational stances: how the organization has decided to interpret a given domain question, along with its constraints, boundary conditions, and machine-actionable routing implications", "why": "position 파일 정의"}
{"id": "e13", "source": "w1", "locator": "§Building the Organizational Second Brain", "quote": "Taxonomy and vocabulary files act as an authoritative glossary for the terms the organization uses to describe its domain", "why": "vocabulary 파일 정의"}
{"id": "e14", "source": "w1", "locator": "§Building the Organizational Second Brain", "quote": "Routing indexes map input characteristics to the relevant positions and procedures, determining which files apply without relying on embedding similarity alone. This makes retrieval deterministic and auditable.", "why": "routing index 정의"}
{"id": "e15", "source": "w1", "locator": "§Building the Organizational Second Brain", "quote": "Gateway files define threshold tests the agent must pass before entering an analytical domain, preventing it from applying specialized knowledge where it does not belong.", "why": "gateway 파일 정의"}
{"id": "e16", "source": "w1", "locator": "§Building the Organizational Second Brain", "quote": "Every file declares its dependencies (depends_on) and consumers (referenced_by) in YAML frontmatter, forming a bidirectional dependency graph.", "why": "양방향 의존 그래프"}
{"id": "e17", "source": "w1", "locator": "§Building the Organizational Second Brain", "quote": "When one file changes, you can trace exactly what else might be affected, which matters when the self-improvement loop proposes automated edits.", "why": "의존 그래프가 자동 편집의 전제"}
{"id": "e18", "source": "w1", "locator": "w1 knowledge-system 그림", "quote": "triggers: # WHEN to load this page", "why": "frontmatter 의 triggers 필드"}
{"id": "e19", "source": "w1", "locator": "w1 knowledge-system 그림", "quote": "SKILL.md ← \"Homepage\" — routes to the right workflow", "why": "그림의 진입 파일 이름이 SKILL.md"}
{"id": "e20", "source": "w1", "locator": "w1 knowledge-system 그림", "quote": "knowledge/positions/ ← Supreme authority articles", "why": "position 이 최상위 권위"}
{"id": "e21", "source": "w1", "locator": "§Organizing Knowledge by Density and Usage Frequency", "quote": "We split on information density and expected usage frequency.", "why": "분할 기준"}
{"id": "e22", "source": "w1", "locator": "§Organizing Knowledge by Density and Usage Frequency", "quote": "High-density, frequently referenced sources go into the wiki: Distilled files capturing how the organization reasons, such as positions, decision frameworks, boundary examples, and strategic interpretations. The agent consults these on nearly every turn.", "why": "wiki 쪽"}
{"id": "e23", "source": "w1", "locator": "§Organizing Knowledge by Density and Usage Frequency", "quote": "Sparse, situationally relevant sources are served through semantic or lexical search (RAG): documents that matter deeply when they apply but are not needed in detail on most runs", "why": "RAG 쪽"}
{"id": "e24", "source": "w1", "locator": "§Organizing Knowledge by Density and Usage Frequency", "quote": "Loading all of them into the wiki would bloat the system and dilute attention.", "why": "전부 wiki 에 넣지 않는 이유"}
{"id": "e25", "source": "w1", "locator": "§Expert Reasoning via Composable Recipes", "quote": "Where knowledge files are declarative, recipes are imperative.", "why": "recipe 정의"}
{"id": "e26", "source": "w1", "locator": "§Expert Reasoning via Composable Recipes", "quote": "Recipes reference knowledge files but contain no domain facts; knowledge files state positions but prescribe no procedures.", "why": "분리 규칙"}
{"id": "e27", "source": "w1", "locator": "§Expert Reasoning via Composable Recipes", "quote": "Adding an organizational position means adding a knowledge file and updating a routing index. No recipe changes.", "why": "변경 국소성 1"}
{"id": "e28", "source": "w1", "locator": "§Expert Reasoning via Composable Recipes", "quote": "Fixing a flaw in the agent’s methodology means editing a recipe. No knowledge files change.", "why": "변경 국소성 2"}
{"id": "e29", "source": "w1", "locator": "§Expert Reasoning via Composable Recipes", "quote": "Failures attribute cleanly to one layer. Was the knowledge wrong, or the procedure?", "why": "귀속 가능성"}
{"id": "e30", "source": "w1", "locator": "§Expert Reasoning via Composable Recipes", "quote": "Our top-level routing recipe examines the input and selects which downstream recipes to invoke, each handling one analytical phase.", "why": "routing recipe"}
{"id": "e31", "source": "w1", "locator": "§Expert Reasoning via Composable Recipes", "quote": "Early versions used a single flat instruction file and loaded all sources via semantic search, pulling a large volume of mixed-relevance files into the context window on every run.", "why": "이전 구조"}
{"id": "e32", "source": "w1", "locator": "§Expert Reasoning via Composable Recipes", "quote": "After restructuring into recipe-driven stages, each query touches only a small, targeted subset, cutting tokens consumed per turn by around 80%.", "why": "80% 숫자와 비교 기준"}
{"id": "e33", "source": "w1", "locator": "§Keeping Humans in Control", "quote": "Checkpoints are defined points in the analysis where the agent surfaces its intermediate reasoning for expert review before proceeding, and the expert can confirm, correct, or redirect.", "why": "checkpoint"}
{"id": "e34", "source": "w1", "locator": "§Keeping Humans in Control", "quote": "Escalations trigger when the agent hits genuine ambiguity, whether from underspecified inputs or evidence that supports more than one defensible reading.", "why": "escalation"}
{"id": "e35", "source": "w1", "locator": "§Keeping Humans in Control", "quote": "Training signal: Every correction and every escalation becomes input for the self-improvement loop.", "why": "교정이 루프 입력"}
{"id": "e36", "source": "w1", "locator": "§The Self-Improvement Flywheel", "quote": "This process can take weeks because it requires understanding the full dependency graph, verifying nothing else breaks, and validating the fix actually works.", "why": "수작업 유지보수 비용"}
{"id": "e37", "source": "w1", "locator": "§The Self-Improvement Flywheel", "quote": "Agents that auto-draft their own fixes are increasingly common; but we haven’t seen this level of validation rigor applied to a structured knowledge base without model retraining.", "why": "Meta 의 새로움 주장"}
{"id": "e38", "source": "w1", "locator": "§The Self-Improvement Flywheel", "quote": "We treat that maintenance as a compilation problem and automate it.", "why": "compilation 비유"}
{"id": "e39", "source": "w1", "locator": "§The Self-Improvement Flywheel", "quote": "Have domain experts review them.", "why": "본문 목록 넷째 phase 는 사람 검토"}
{"id": "e40", "source": "w1", "locator": "§Diagnosis", "quote": "This heuristic failed because conversational form is a poor proxy for root cause.", "why": "첫 접근의 실패"}
{"id": "e41", "source": "w1", "locator": "§Diagnosis", "quote": "First, extract every substantive signal from the expert alongside the agent’s full knowledge manifest (every file loaded, when, and how used).", "why": "manifest"}
{"id": "e42", "source": "w1", "locator": "§Diagnosis", "quote": "Could the agent have reached the correct conclusion from its source materials?", "why": "귀속 테스트 질문"}
{"id": "e43", "source": "w1", "locator": "§Diagnosis", "quote": "If the materials contained the right answer but the agent still erred: recipe problem.", "why": "분기 1"}
{"id": "e44", "source": "w1", "locator": "§Diagnosis", "quote": "If the materials did not contain the right answer: knowledge gap.", "why": "분기 2"}
{"id": "e45", "source": "w1", "locator": "§Diagnosis", "quote": "If experts themselves disagree on the right answer: ambiguity, flagged for human discussion.", "why": "분기 3"}
{"id": "e46", "source": "w1", "locator": "w1 루프 그림 Phase 1", "quote": "Weight By Frequency And Severity", "why": "그림에만 있는 가중 단계"}
{"id": "e47", "source": "w1", "locator": "§Compilation", "quote": "Sub-agents analyze impact in parallel, examining cross-references, conflicts with existing positions, token budget impact, test coverage, and duplication risk.", "why": "병렬 영향 분석"}
{"id": "e48", "source": "w1", "locator": "§Compilation", "quote": "A separate agent, running in a fresh context with no knowledge of the improvement rationale, receives only the proposed diffs to the knowledge base.", "why": "적대적 리뷰어 입력"}
{"id": "e49", "source": "w1", "locator": "§Compilation", "quote": "Because it shares no context with the proposing agents, it cannot inherit their blind spots.", "why": "분리의 이유"}
{"id": "e50", "source": "w1", "locator": "§Compilation", "quote": "A linter catches issues programmatically, dangling cross-references, file size budget violations, identifier collisions, and dependency cycles. This layer is not probabilistic. It passes or fails.", "why": "결정적 linter"}
{"id": "e51", "source": "w1", "locator": "§Evaluation", "quote": "Targeted replay runs the agent on the original scenario that triggered the feedback. The agent does not know it is being tested.", "why": "targeted replay"}
{"id": "e52", "source": "w1", "locator": "§Evaluation", "quote": "A separate judge evaluates the new output against the original expert feedback without knowing what was changed.", "why": "blind judge"}
{"id": "e53", "source": "w1", "locator": "§Evaluation", "quote": "Regression testing runs multiple benchmarks for that domain, which are usually structured test suites of Q&A pairs.", "why": "회귀 벤치마크 형태"}
{"id": "e54", "source": "w1", "locator": "§Evaluation", "quote": "an independent LLM judge gives each test case a pass/fail based on certain criteria", "why": "판정자도 LLM"}
{"id": "e55", "source": "w1", "locator": "§Evaluation", "quote": "If regression testing fails, compilation is retried with an updated prompt describing where the agent regressed, along with the original issue and attempted fix.", "why": "재시도 프롬프트"}
{"id": "e56", "source": "w1", "locator": "§Landing and Enrichment", "quote": "The output of the pipeline is a pull request (diff) with a complete audit trail. A human expert reviews a proven fix rather than debugging a raw failure.", "why": "PR 로 착지"}
{"id": "e57", "source": "w1", "locator": "§Landing and Enrichment", "quote": "the original failing scenario and its validated correct answer are automatically added to the regression test suite", "why": "보강"}
{"id": "e58", "source": "w1", "locator": "§Results", "quote": "After three development sprints spanning six weeks, the system achieved:", "why": "결과 기간"}
{"id": "e59", "source": "w1", "locator": "§Results", "quote": "Domain SMEs rated agent outputs useful almost all the time", "why": "결과 1 정성"}
{"id": "e60", "source": "w1", "locator": "§Results", "quote": "Days to minutes reduction in individual assessment time.", "why": "결과 2"}
{"id": "e61", "source": "w1", "locator": "§Results", "quote": "Automated self-improvement producing validated knowledge edits at a rate that previously required full engineering sprints.", "why": "결과 3"}
{"id": "e62", "source": "w1", "locator": "§Results", "quote": "Zero regressions across improvement cycles, with every fix automatically strengthening the regression suite.", "why": "결과 4"}
{"id": "e63", "source": "w1", "locator": "§Applying This Architecture", "quote": "Specialist knowledge lives as tribal knowledge in experts’ heads.", "why": "적용 조건 1"}
{"id": "e64", "source": "w1", "locator": "§Applying This Architecture", "quote": "Off-the-shelf LLMs produce inadequate analysis.", "why": "적용 조건 4"}
{"id": "e65", "source": "w1", "locator": "§Applying This Architecture", "quote": "keep the complexity in text files that are readable by both humans and agents, rather than fine-tuned model weights", "why": "핵심 원리"}
{"id": "e66", "source": "w1", "locator": "§Applying This Architecture", "quote": "Every improvement is a text edit that a domain expert can review in 30 seconds. Every change is version-controlled, diffable, and reversible.", "why": "30초, 버전 관리"}
{"id": "e67", "source": "w2", "locator": "§Code is no longer the bottleneck", "quote": "Build is no longer the constraint — the human-speed steps around it are.", "why": "playbook 의 전제"}
{"id": "e68", "source": "w2", "locator": "§What is an AI-native SDLC?", "quote": "The AI-native SDLC is a reimagined process that combines the old control objectives with new enforcement. Instead of a linear flow, the process becomes a loop, and AI is embedded at each point.", "why": "정의"}
{"id": "e69", "source": "w2", "locator": "§What is an AI-native SDLC?", "quote": "The thread running through the right-hand column is the committed artifact.", "why": "committed artifact"}
{"id": "e70", "source": "w2", "locator": "§What is an AI-native SDLC?", "quote": "The chain of commits is also the audit trail: who asked for what, what the agent produced, and who approved it.", "why": "audit trail"}
{"id": "e71", "source": "w2", "locator": "§Build · The CLAUDE.md", "quote": "Knowledge that used to sit in people's heads and on wikis becomes a file the agent reads at the start of every session, maintained by the whole team and iterated on whenever a mistake is made.", "why": "CLAUDE.md 가 지식 파일"}
{"id": "e72", "source": "w2", "locator": "§Build · The CLAUDE.md", "quote": "When Claude makes a mistake twice, the correction goes into CLAUDE.md.", "why": "두 번 규칙"}
{"id": "e73", "source": "w2", "locator": "§Build · The CLAUDE.md", "quote": "Keep it under a page, because Claude reads all of it at the start of a session and anything stale is taking up context for no benefit.", "why": "한 쪽 이하"}
{"id": "e74", "source": "w2", "locator": "§Build · Skills as institutional knowledge", "quote": "Skills are how an organization makes its institutional knowledge operational. The instructions are explicit, version-controlled, applied broadly, and updated centrally when policy changes.", "why": "skills 가 제도 지식"}
{"id": "e75", "source": "w2", "locator": "§Build · Skills as institutional knowledge", "quote": "Write it as a skill, a folder containing a SKILL.md whose frontmatter says when it triggers and whose body says what to do.", "why": "SKILL.md frontmatter trigger"}
{"id": "e76", "source": "w2", "locator": "§Build · Skills as institutional knowledge", "quote": "When the policy changes, change the skill and have the policy owner sign off the change.", "why": "정책 소유자 서명"}
{"id": "e77", "source": "w2", "locator": "§Build · Skills as institutional knowledge", "quote": "A skill is a control, though an advisory one. It makes Claude likely to apply the policy while the code is written, and nothing forces a session to comply with it.", "why": "advisory control"}
{"id": "e78", "source": "w2", "locator": "§Build · Skills as institutional knowledge", "quote": "Where the findings don't fall towards zero, either the skill isn't triggering or its text has drifted from the official policy.", "why": "skill drift 측정"}
{"id": "e79", "source": "w2", "locator": "§Test · Give Claude a feedback loop", "quote": "This way the verdict is not colored by the assumptions that produced the code.", "why": "fresh context verifier"}
{"id": "e80", "source": "w2", "locator": "§Test · Give Claude a feedback loop", "quote": "Finally, the loop itself needs protecting, because an agent fixing code must not be able to weaken the check on that code.", "why": "검사 보호"}
{"id": "e81", "source": "w2", "locator": "§Test · Continuous evals in CI", "quote": "When a new model is swapped in or a prompt is rewritten, the eval suite says whether the agent still does the work to the same standard.", "why": "config 회귀"}
{"id": "e82", "source": "w2", "locator": "§Test · Continuous evals in CI", "quote": "The platform engineer collects 20 to 50 real tasks from recent work with its expected/accepted outcome.", "why": "eval 규모"}
{"id": "e83", "source": "w2", "locator": "§Test · Continuous evals in CI", "quote": "The suite runs non-interactively in CI on a schedule and on any change to CLAUDE.md, skills or hooks, since that configuration steers the agent and deserves the regression testing that code gets.", "why": "설정도 회귀 테스트"}
{"id": "e84", "source": "w2", "locator": "§Test · Continuous evals in CI", "quote": "Each production incident gets an eval, written by the team that owned the incident, and stays in the suite as a regression test.", "why": "incident → eval"}
{"id": "e85", "source": "w2", "locator": "§Test · Continuous evals in CI", "quote": "As models improve, cases that once discriminated stop doing so and new ones must be added that arise from ongoing monitoring.", "why": "eval 수명"}
{"id": "e86", "source": "w2", "locator": "§Deploy · AI in the PR review loop", "quote": "Separation of duties is preserved, because the agent that wrote the code has no way to approve it.", "why": "직무 분리"}
{"id": "e87", "source": "w2", "locator": "§Deploy · AI in the PR review loop", "quote": "Review findings feed back into CLAUDE.md. When a review flags a mistake for the second time, the correction goes into CLAUDE.md as part of that review", "why": "리뷰 → CLAUDE.md"}
{"id": "e88", "source": "w2", "locator": "§Deploy · CI/CD integration and deployment", "quote": "Rollback should be the most rehearsed path in the pipeline", "why": "rollback"}
{"id": "e89", "source": "w2", "locator": "§Maintain", "quote": "Stage 6: Maintenance runs headless, with an independent confidence gate between stages, a deterministic check or an adversarial reviewing agent, deciding whether the previous stage's output continues or is escalated to a human.", "why": "독립 confidence gate"}
{"id": "e90", "source": "w2", "locator": "§Maintain · Closing the loop", "quote": "The script is version controlled and unit tested, and detection stays entirely deterministic, with no model involved.", "why": "결정적 탐지"}
{"id": "e91", "source": "w2", "locator": "§Maintain · Closing the loop", "quote": "When a fix ships, add an eval for the incident (the continuous evals play) to ensure that such issues are protected against going forwards.", "why": "fix → eval"}
{"id": "e92", "source": "w2", "locator": "§Closing thoughts", "quote": "The loop keeps running. Human judgement stays above it.", "why": "맺음"}
{"id": "e93", "source": "w3", "locator": "§The core idea", "quote": "The knowledge is compiled once and then *kept current*, not re-derived on every query.", "why": "LLM Wiki 핵심"}
{"id": "e94", "source": "w3", "locator": "§Architecture", "quote": "**The schema** — a document (e.g. CLAUDE.md for Claude Code or AGENTS.md for Codex) that tells the LLM how the wiki is structured", "why": "schema 층"}
{"id": "e95", "source": "w3", "locator": "§Operations", "quote": "**Lint.** Periodically, ask the LLM to health-check the wiki. Look for: contradictions between pages, stale claims that newer sources have superseded, orphan pages with no inbound links", "why": "Karpathy 의 lint"}
{"id": "e96", "source": "w3", "locator": "§Indexing and logging", "quote": "This works surprisingly well at moderate scale (~100 sources, ~hundreds of pages) and avoids the need for embedding-based RAG infrastructure.", "why": "index 로 충분한 규모"}
{"id": "e97", "source": "w3", "locator": "§Why this works", "quote": "The wiki stays maintained because the cost of maintenance is near zero.", "why": "유지비 주장"}
{"id": "e98", "source": "w3", "locator": "§The core idea", "quote": "You never (or rarely) write the wiki yourself — the LLM writes and maintains all of it.", "why": "LLM 이 소유"}
{"id": "e99", "source": "w4", "locator": "§intro", "quote": "an open specification that formalizes the LLM-wiki pattern into a portable, interoperable format", "why": "OKF 정의"}
{"id": "e100", "source": "w4", "locator": "§Three principles", "quote": "OKF requires exactly one thing of every concept: a type field.", "why": "최소 요구"}
{"id": "e101", "source": "w4", "locator": "§How OKF works", "quote": "Bundles can optionally include index.md files (for progressive disclosure as agents navigate the hierarchy) and log.md files (for chronological history of changes).", "why": "progressive disclosure 용 index.md"}
{"id": "e102", "source": "c1", "locator": "§Key terms", "quote": "Gate: the rule that decides whether a proposed skill edit should become the current skill.", "why": "gate 정의"}
{"id": "e103", "source": "c1", "locator": "§3.1", "quote": "In a paired study with gpt-5.4-nano on SearchQA, the ungated run adopted a plausible but wrong rule—answer with the document title string verbatim—and fell from 55.4% to 2.6%. The gated run rejected all proposals and remained flat at 57.0%.", "why": "무게이트 붕괴 사례"}
{"id": "e104", "source": "c1", "locator": "§3.1", "quote": "The two runs started from different measured baselines, so this is not evidence that they encountered identical candidate edits; it is an observed stress-case contrast.", "why": "저자 단서"}
{"id": "e105", "source": "c1", "locator": "§Part II", "quote": "that judgment can route a likely Skill Defect toward a targeted skill-body update and an Execution Lapse toward a protected appendix reminder", "why": "결함 귀속 두 갈래"}
{"id": "e106", "source": "c1", "locator": "§2.1", "quote": "gpt-5.4-mini | Spreadsheet | -13.8% | +4.7%", "why": "넓은 기억이 작은 모델을 망침"}
{"id": "e107", "source": "c1", "locator": "§2.2", "quote": "the absolute score changes are +9.65% on mini SearchQA, +15.00% on mini SpreadsheetBench, and +2.32% on nano SpreadsheetBench", "why": "consolidation 회복"}
{"id": "e108", "source": "c1", "locator": "§Part III", "quote": "Normal operation does not replace the deployed skill until the user explicitly runs adopt; auto_adopt is an opt-in mode.", "why": "staged adoption"}
{"id": "e109", "source": "c1", "locator": "§Evidence and reproducibility boundary", "quote": "Its raw per-run artifacts are not included in the public repository, so this post is not a reproduction package for those ablations.", "why": "재현 한계"}
{"id": "e110", "source": "c1", "locator": "§3.4", "quote": "The Sleep study is single-seed per cell; treat differences below 1.5 percentage points as noise", "why": "단일 seed"}
{"id": "e111", "source": "c2", "locator": "§intro", "quote": "Employees ask our internal knowledge base more than 15,000 questions every day.", "why": "Cerebras 규모"}
{"id": "e112", "source": "c2", "locator": "§core", "quote": "At the core is a single Postgres table that holds embeddings, raw summaries, and metadata from many sources.", "why": "단일 embeddings 표"}
{"id": "e113", "source": "c2", "locator": "§Slack", "quote": "Information density varies enormously: “hey yeah sure mike” and a detailed kernel explanation are both messages.", "why": "밀도 변이"}
{"id": "e114", "source": "c2", "locator": "§Slack", "quote": "During distillation, an LLM extracts structured data from the full thread:", "why": "증류"}
{"id": "e115", "source": "c2", "locator": "§Slack", "quote": "The original transcript is not embedded directly. In our experiments, accuracy increased significantly when the thread was normalized into a consistent format.", "why": "정규화 효과"}
{"id": "e116", "source": "c2", "locator": "§Slack", "quote": "encodes that Slack answers expire. Two threads can answer the same question, and the one from six months ago may describe infrastructure that no longer exists.", "why": "신선도"}
{"id": "e117", "source": "c2", "locator": "§Projects", "quote": "As the corpus grew, “search everything everywhere” rapidly stopped being useful.", "why": "검색 범위 좁히기"}
{"id": "e118", "source": "c3", "locator": "§intro", "quote": "Claude authors about 80% of the code merged into our codebase today.", "why": "Anthropic 맥락 숫자"}
{"id": "e119", "source": "c3", "locator": "§Code", "quote": "At Anthropic, those guidelines are encoded in CLAUDE.md files and references to org-wide skills so the code follows these best practices the minute it's generated. This is done as part of a closed loop. Once an agent discovers a bug class, the relevant file is updated to prevent it recurring in future code.", "why": "bug class → 파일 갱신"}
{"id": "e120", "source": "c3", "locator": "§Test (CI)", "quote": "The share of PRs that get substantive review comments has grown from 16 to 54% as we’ve gained confidence in the findings by requiring the agents to write a proof that their finding is valid.", "why": "증명 요구"}
{"id": "e121", "source": "c3", "locator": "§Test (CI)", "quote": "They do not share biases and blindspots", "why": "좁은 리뷰어 분리"}
{"id": "e122", "source": "c3", "locator": "§Governance", "quote": "If a skill goes stale, a discovered bug class never makes it back into CLAUDE.md, or an agent's decisions go unsampled, the whole structure degrades.", "why": "지식 파일 부패 위험"}
{"id": "e123", "source": "c3", "locator": "§Governance", "quote": "Shadow mode for all new AI reviewers. New agents post comments for human approval until trust is earned.", "why": "shadow mode"}
{"id": "e124", "source": "c3", "locator": "§Monitor", "quote": "Following a model upgrade, the incident response agent reached out over Slack to another Claude instance on its own initiative. It asked the agent, which could write code, to push the fix.", "why": "경계 사건"}
{"id": "e125", "source": "c3", "locator": "§Monitor", "quote": "this experience taught us to draw the boundary around access and actions, not around a model’s instructions or what we believe a model can do", "why": "지시가 아니라 권한으로 경계"}
{"id": "e126", "source": "c4", "locator": "§meta", "quote": "DateAugust 18, 2026", "why": "날짜"}
{"id": "e127", "source": "c4", "locator": "§Our Claude on call setup", "quote": "Standing instructions are in markdown files as skills, committed in a GitHub repository. This way multiple teammates can iterate on them and we can manage changes just like we do code.", "why": "지식 파일을 코드처럼"}
{"id": "e128", "source": "c4", "locator": "§Our Claude on call setup", "quote": "It also includes key information like routing instructions, policies, and a log of lessons learned as part of a self-improvement loop.", "why": "routing + lessons"}
{"id": "e129", "source": "c4", "locator": "§Detection", "quote": "goes through the criteria in the root oncall.md file to determine if it can wait until the morning or if the on-call needs a page", "why": "oncall.md 가 gateway 같은 문턱"}
{"id": "e130", "source": "c4", "locator": "§Triage", "quote": "For example, a 617 line investigation skill for shadow divergence bugs encodes every step I take during a typical investigation.", "why": "617줄 skill"}
{"id": "e131", "source": "c4", "locator": "§Triage", "quote": "Lessons.md also guides Claude’s troubleshooting. This markdown file is a running log of every incident we've resolved: what happened, the root cause, the fix, and the gotcha worth remembering. Claude appends to it on its own automatically.", "why": "lessons.md 자동 추가"}
{"id": "e132", "source": "c4", "locator": "§Triage", "quote": "If the same pattern shows up enough times, we promote it into the investigation skill itself.", "why": "승격"}
{"id": "e133", "source": "c4", "locator": "§Triage", "quote": "query the data first, then theorize. Config tells you what could go wrong; metrics tell you what did.", "why": "lessons 항목 예"}
{"id": "e134", "source": "c4", "locator": "§Triage", "quote": "Claude posts its first evidence-grounded analysis a median of 14 minutes after an incident opens", "why": "on-call 숫자"}
{"id": "e135", "source": "c4", "locator": "§Verification", "quote": "One honest note: we needed to iterate the report format several times.", "why": "반복 필요"}
{"id": "e136", "source": "w2", "locator": "§Test · Give Claude a feedback loop · Who approves", "quote": "The code owner reviewing the PR, who can concentrate on intent and risk because the mechanical evidence is already attached.", "why": "사람의 자리 일치"}
{"id": "e137", "source": "w2", "locator": "§Test · Give Claude a feedback loop", "quote": "For bug fixes, write the failing test first.", "why": "시험 먼저"}
{"id": "e138", "source": "w2", "locator": "§Build · plan mode", "quote": "When implementation departs from the plan, update plan.md in the same commit.", "why": "의도된 변경과 산출물 동기화"}
{"id": "e139", "source": "w2", "locator": "§Test · Continuous evals in CI", "quote": "Write each task as an eval, meaning the prompt plus the checks that define acceptable (tests pass, lint clean, behavior unchanged, policy followed).", "why": "eval 판정 기준"}
{"id": "e140", "source": "w2", "locator": "§Maintain · Closing the loop", "quote": "Detection stays deterministic. Claude is invoked once a band is breached, and the tier sets what it may do.", "why": "결정적 탐지 2"}
{"id": "e141", "source": "w1", "locator": "§The Self-Improvement Flywheel", "quote": "much less attention has gone toward keeping a document-based institutional knowledge base correct as it grows and as expert positions evolve", "why": "입장 변화 인지"}
{"id": "e142", "source": "w1", "locator": "§The Self-Improvement Flywheel", "quote": "We consider the self-improvement flywheel to be the most distinctive part of this system.", "why": "가장 독특한 부분"}
{"id": "e143", "source": "w1", "locator": "w1 표 그림", "quote": "LLMs are better at managing knowledge than people.", "why": "근거 없는 착안 문장"}
{"id": "e144", "source": "w1", "locator": "w1 knowledge-system 그림", "quote": "Generalized example — any domain expert agent", "why": "그림이 일반화 예시임"}
{"id": "e145", "source": "w1", "locator": "w1 루프 그림", "quote": "Phase 4: Landing And Enrichment", "why": "그림의 넷째 phase"}
{"id": "e146", "source": "w1", "locator": "§intro", "quote": "We set about solving this challenge by codifying institutional intelligence into an AI agent for a specific compliance domain.", "why": "도메인 이름 없음"}
{"id": "e147", "source": "c1", "locator": "§1.1", "quote": "These observations motivate treating hard gating as a stability control rather than assuming one policy dominates every target and task.", "why": "gate 를 안정성 통제로"}
{"id": "e148", "source": "c4", "locator": "§Triage", "quote": "My favorite entry is one Claude wrote about me.", "why": "lessons 예의 맥락"}
{"id": "e149", "source": "w2", "locator": "§Build · The CLAUDE.md", "quote": "## Things Claude gets wrong", "why": "CLAUDE.md 예시에 섞인 항목"}
{"id": "e150", "source": "w1", "locator": "§Compilation: Surgical Multi-Agent Edits", "quote": "Its job is to find problems such as contradictions introduced, edge cases broken, or positions undermined.", "why": "적대적 리뷰어가 찾는 문제: 모순, 경계 사례, 약해진 입장"}
{"id": "e151", "source": "w1", "locator": "§Building the Organizational Second Brain", "quote": "Taxonomy and vocabulary files act as an authoritative glossary for the terms the organization uses to describe its domain", "why": "vocabulary 파일의 정의"}
{"id": "e152", "source": "w1", "locator": "§Organizing Knowledge by Density and Usage Frequency", "quote": "Because they encode the organization’s evolving thinking, they need to stay current, and the wiki structure makes them easy to update, version, and validate.", "why": "wiki 쪽 파일은 현재 상태를 유지해야 한다"}
{"id": "e153", "source": "w2", "locator": "§Stage 3: Build / Review (PR review play)", "quote": "Review also flags when a change has made CLAUDE.md outdated.", "why": "리뷰가 CLAUDE.md 가 낡았음을 표시한다"}
{"id": "e154", "source": "w2", "locator": "§Continuous evals in CI", "quote": "Gate configuration changes on the results. A skill change that drops the pass rate gets reviewed before it merges.", "why": "설정 변경의 gate: 통과율이 떨어지면 리뷰"}
{"id": "e155", "source": "w2", "locator": "§The CLAUDE.md, How to measure it", "quote": "How often Claude repeats a mistake CLAUDE.md should have caught.", "why": "곁 루프의 지표는 반복된 실수"}
{"id": "e156", "source": "w2", "locator": "§The CLAUDE.md", "quote": "Check CLAUDE.md into git at the repo root so the whole team shares one version and changes are reviewed like code.", "why": "CLAUDE.md 를 코드처럼 리뷰"}
{"id": "e157", "source": "w2", "locator": "§Skills", "quote": "The rule of thumb: write a skill for institutional knowledge that must be applied consistently; don't write a skill for components that belong in CLAUDE.md or a prompt.", "why": "skill 과 CLAUDE.md 의 경계 규칙"}
{"id": "e158", "source": "w2", "locator": "§Closing the loop (Stage 6)", "quote": "Claude diagnoses, acts only through gated routes, and writes what it finds as intent.md, which then goes through the stages described above.", "why": "Maintain 의 신호는 band 위반 등 트리거"}
{"id": "e159", "source": "d1", "locator": "§CLAUDE.md vs auto memory", "quote": "Claude treats them as context, not enforced configuration. To block an action regardless of what Claude decides, use a [PreToolUse hook](/docs/en/hooks-guide) instead.", "why": "CLAUDE.md 는 강제 설정이 아니다, 강제는 hook"}
{"id": "e160", "source": "d1", "locator": "§CLAUDE.md vs auto memory", "quote": "Auto memory lets Claude learn from your corrections without manual effort.", "why": "auto memory 는 교정을 사람 손 없이 적는다"}
{"id": "e161", "source": "d1", "locator": "§When to add to CLAUDE.md", "quote": "A code review catches something Claude should have known about this codebase", "why": "CLAUDE.md 에 추가할 신호: 코드 리뷰"}
{"id": "e162", "source": "d1", "locator": "§When to add to CLAUDE.md", "quote": "Consistency**: if two instructions contradict each other, Claude may pick one arbitrarily.", "why": "두 지시가 모순되면 임의로 고른다"}
{"id": "e163", "source": "d1", "locator": "§Audit your instruction files", "quote": "Claude looks for problems such as instructions written for older models, references to files or commands that don't exist, and files that contradict each other. You get a report of findings with proposed edits, and nothing in your files changes until you ask Claude to apply them.", "why": "prompt-audit: 낡은 지시와 모순을 찾아 제안만 한다"}
{"id": "e164", "source": "d1", "locator": "§Auto memory", "quote": "Claude skips anything it can derive from the codebase, such as architecture, file paths, or debugging fixes. It also skips anything your CLAUDE.md files already say.", "why": "auto memory 가 적지 않는 것"}
{"id": "e165", "source": "d1", "locator": "§How it works", "quote": "If the file is near a limit, Claude Code reminds Claude to shorten it: keep one line per entry, move detail into topic files, and merge or drop stale entries.", "why": "auto memory 의 정리 규칙"}
{"id": "e166", "source": "d2", "locator": "§intro", "quote": "Create a skill when you keep pasting the same instructions, checklist, or multi-step procedure into chat, or when a section of CLAUDE.md has grown into a procedure rather than a fact. Unlike CLAUDE.md content, a skill's body loads only when it's used, so long reference material costs almost nothing until you need it.", "why": "사실은 CLAUDE.md, 절차는 skill 이라는 문서의 경계"}
{"id": "e167", "source": "w5", "locator": "§1 Motivation", "quote": "Increasingly, a knowledge corpus is not authored once and then read: it\nis **continuously written and maintained by agents**.", "why": "OKF v0.2 의 동기: agent 가 계속 쓰는 corpus"}
{"id": "e168", "source": "w5", "locator": "§5.2 Trust", "quote": "They are kept distinct because who *wrote* a concept need not\nbe who *confirmed* it.", "why": "작성자와 확인자를 분리하는 필드"}
{"id": "e169", "source": "w5", "locator": "§5.4 Lifecycle: status", "quote": "- `deprecated`: kept for links and history; no longer current.", "why": "deprecated 상태"}
{"id": "e170", "source": "w5", "locator": "§5.5 Lifecycle: stale_after", "quote": "Optional. An absolute instant. A concept is stale when\n`now >= stale_after`.", "why": "stale_after"}
{"id": "e171", "source": "w5", "locator": "§6.1 Links between concepts", "quote": "The specific\nkind (parent/child, references, joins-with, depends-on) is conveyed by the\nsurrounding prose, not by the link itself.", "why": "OKF 링크는 종류가 없다"}
{"id": "e172", "source": "w5", "locator": "§6.1 Links between concepts", "quote": "Consumers MUST tolerate broken links: a link whose target does not exist\nin the bundle is not malformed; it may simply represent not-yet-written\nknowledge.", "why": "OKF 는 끊긴 링크를 허용한다 (Meta linter 와 반대)"}
{"id": "e173", "source": "w5", "locator": "§5.3 Trust tiers", "quote": "Trust tiers are advisory signals, not access control.", "why": "trust tier 는 권고"}
{"id": "e174", "source": "c5", "locator": "§Why Contract Review is Harder Than it Looks", "quote": "Standard position: the ideal term a company wants to see in their contracts", "why": "playbook 규칙의 standard position"}
{"id": "e175", "source": "c5", "locator": "§Why Contract Review is Harder Than it Looks", "quote": "Rules interact across a document: A single rule about assignment rights can touch four different sections in the document and at the same time, another rule might propose an edit on the same sentence creating a conflict.", "why": "규칙끼리 같은 문장에서 충돌"}
{"id": "e176", "source": "c5", "locator": "§Why Contract Review is Harder Than it Looks", "quote": "Some decisions cannot be delegated: A playbook alone cannot capture the nuance of deal.", "why": "위임할 수 없는 결정"}
{"id": "e177", "source": "c5", "locator": "§Our First System: A Pipeline of Prompts", "quote": "Every rule was evaluated independently, so two rules could propose contradictory edits to the same sentence, and there was no rewriting for those edge cases.", "why": "옛 시스템의 충돌 문제"}
{"id": "e178", "source": "c5", "locator": "§Making Legal Judgment Measurable", "quote": "After sourcing the rubrics with lawyers, we set up an evaluation framework that uses LLM judges to score against these rubrics. We then used a committee of three frontier models to score independently and aggregate the votes.", "why": "변호사 rubric + LLM judge 3개 위원회"}
{"id": "e179", "source": "c5", "locator": "§Orchestrator Agent With Subagents", "quote": "When subagents finish, a reconciliation step merges branches the same way a version-control system would: non-conflicting edits apply cleanly to the final doc, and collisions of two rules touching the same text are escalated for the lead agent to resolve.", "why": "충돌은 lead agent 로 escalation"}
{"id": "e180", "source": "c5", "locator": "§Orchestrator Agent With Subagents", "quote": "resolve conflicts in the document the way a senior lawyer would by drafting edits that satisfies all conflicting rules", "why": "충돌 해소 방식"}
{"id": "e181", "source": "c5", "locator": "§Eval Results", "quote": "Redline rubric\n|\n53%\n|\n87%\n|\n+34%", "why": "redline rubric 53 → 87"}
{"id": "e182", "source": "c5", "locator": "§Eval Results", "quote": "Risk classification\n|\n59%\n|\n77%\n|\n+18%", "why": "risk classification 59 → 77"}
{"id": "e183", "source": "c5", "locator": "§What Agentic Review Unlocks", "quote": "Closing the loop with self-improvement becomes possible. Every accepted, edited, or rejected redline helps agents understand a legal team's preferences.", "why": "Harvey 의 자기 개선은 아직 앞으로의 일"}
{"id": "e184", "source": "c5", "locator": "§Why Contract Review is Harder Than it Looks", "quote": "The best edit is usually the smallest one", "why": "최소 편집이 품질 기준"}
{"id": "e185", "source": "c6", "locator": "§intro", "quote": "Duet and Autopilot now author 70% of merged AOP lines across production teams.", "why": "자동 작성 비율"}
{"id": "e186", "source": "c6", "locator": "§Simulation generation self-heals over time", "quote": "Self-improving agents carry an easy-to-miss dependency: their improvements are judged against test Simulations (sims). Previously, humans would spend hours crafting golden test sets, but a fully self-improving system must write its own sims.", "why": "시험도 시스템이 쓴다"}
{"id": "e187", "source": "c6", "locator": "§Simulation generation self-heals over time", "quote": "Since the judge determines whether an Autopilot fix is truly “correct”, we checked it against human-labeled ground truth and real production outcomes. Similar to sim improvement, judge quality quickly rose in August, reaching 99.5% accuracy.", "why": "judge 정확도를 사람 label 에 대어 쟀다"}
{"id": "e188", "source": "c6", "locator": "§More than 85% of the updates", "quote": "Nearly half of all changes remained fully intact after the first week. Over longer periods, complete reversions or removals represented less than 15% of changes, as teams were more likely to build on or reshape the original edit.", "why": "변경의 지속률과 되돌림"}
{"id": "e189", "source": "c6", "locator": "§Compounding self-improvement", "quote": "Autopilot traced the cause to overly permissive polling instructions, tightened the exit conditions, and shipped a fix that passed simulations and regression testing before reaching human review.", "why": "진단-수정-회귀-사람 검토 순서"}
{"id": "e190", "source": "c6", "locator": "§Duet Autopilot achieved a 81.9% pass rate", "quote": "Broader task coverage: Evaluation includes converting agents to newer architectures, updating agents for changed business requirements, and reducing latency without altering behavior", "why": "요구가 바뀐 경우를 과제로 둔다"}
{"id": "e191", "source": "c6", "locator": "§Resolution rate increased by 25pp", "quote": "At a Fortune 50 enterprise, Autopilot improved a Decagon agent's resolution rate from 30% to 55%.", "why": "결과 수치(자기 보고)"}
{"id": "e192", "source": "p1", "locator": "§3.2 Failure diagnosis", "quote": "Diagnosis uses two LLM stages. The first reads the question, failed answer,\njudge feedback, and retrieved context.", "why": "진단 두 단계"}
{"id": "e193", "source": "p1", "locator": "§3.2 Failure diagnosis", "quote": "Deterministic grep executes this plan.", "why": "가설을 grep 으로 원자료에 대조"}
{"id": "e194", "source": "p1", "locator": "§3.2 Skill proposal", "quote": "The proposer may revise a skill instead of adding one, keeping\nthe registry small and avoids conflicts.", "why": "추가 대신 수정"}
{"id": "e195", "source": "p1", "locator": "§3.3 Gated Promotion", "quote": "Every Correct verdict on $\\mathcal{P}$ under $\\widehat{\\mathcal{S}}$ must remain Correct\nunder $\\mathcal{S}'$.", "why": "보호 suite 회귀 0"}
{"id": "e196", "source": "p1", "locator": "§3.3 Gated Promotion", "quote": "\\emph{Negative controls} test for unwanted activation on no-op,\nmulti-period, and cross-company queries outside the skill's scope.", "why": "negative control"}
{"id": "e197", "source": "p1", "locator": "§3.3 Gated Promotion", "quote": "A promoted skill enters the registry with a version number.\nA revised version supersedes the earlier one, which becomes inactive.\nA skill whose behavior is absorbed by another and that stops activating\nis retired after a removal test.", "why": "버전, 대체, 제거 시험 후 퇴역"}
{"id": "e198", "source": "p1", "locator": "§3.3 Gated Promotion", "quote": "Candidates may also be refused or deferred for insufficient benefit,\nunstable triggering, or conflict with an active skill", "why": "충돌 후보 거절"}
{"id": "e199", "source": "p1", "locator": "§5.4 Evolution Dynamics", "quote": "Only six of 33 proposed skills were promoted. Five candidates failed protected-set checks, exposing seven regressions, while post-round evaluation found no protected regressions in the deployed registry.", "why": "33개 중 6개, 보호 시험 실패 5개"}
{"id": "e200", "source": "p1", "locator": "§5.4 Evolution Dynamics", "quote": "the non-correct rate fell from 30.0\\% to 18.3\\% on the evolution set and from 20.0\\% to 12.5\\% on the monitoring set", "why": "12 라운드 결과"}
{"id": "e201", "source": "p1", "locator": "§Limitations", "quote": "Conservative gates slow adaptation: 27 of 33 candidates were refused,\ndeferred, or withdrawn", "why": "보수적 gate 의 비용"}
{"id": "e202", "source": "p1", "locator": "§Limitations", "quote": "The financial-expert review route was not staffed, so admission decisions\nrested on the automatic checks, and the judge-agreement study uses annotators\nfrom the author group rather than independent domain experts.", "why": "사람 검토 경로가 비어 있었다"}
{"id": "e203", "source": "p1", "locator": "§Limitations", "quote": "its evaluation set was monitored every round, so it\nmeasures how the deployment improved rather than the isolated effect of skill\ntext, and it does not establish blind generalization.", "why": "저자가 인정하는 한계"}
{"id": "e204", "source": "p1", "locator": "부록 Twelve-Round, Interactions between skills", "quote": "Static checks stopped redundant or contradictory proposals before\nadmission.", "why": "정적 검사로 모순 후보 차단"}
{"id": "e205", "source": "p1", "locator": "부록 Table: Conflict handling", "quote": "Blanket abstention on conflicting evidence contradicted the slot skill's requirement to explain gaps and provide the supported answer.", "why": "Conflict-C5 사례"}
{"id": "e206", "source": "p1", "locator": "부록 Table: Conflict handling", "quote": "Calculation instructions overrode unit declarations when both skills were active.", "why": "Conflict-C4 사례"}
{"id": "e207", "source": "p1", "locator": "부록 Table: Conflict handling", "quote": "Give calculation instructions priority on calculation queries, retain their unit-check fields, and use the unit skill for auxiliary checking.", "why": "Conflict-C4 해소: 우선순위 규칙"}
{"id": "e208", "source": "p1", "locator": "부록 Table: Lifecycle", "quote": "At R12, the fusion skill covered its fallback behavior; a removal test found zero protected regressions, and v1 was retired.", "why": "퇴역의 실제 사례"}
{"id": "e209", "source": "p1", "locator": "부록 Twelve-Round Record", "quote": "a protected suite of\n120 questions (90 previously correct and 30 high-risk cases)", "why": "보호 suite 구성"}
{"id": "e210", "source": "p1", "locator": "부록 Judge--Human Agreement", "quote": "Two annotators from the author group independently judged a mixed\nsample of 150 answers against gold answers and key points.", "why": "judge-사람 일치 표본"}
{"id": "e211", "source": "p1", "locator": "부록 Judge--Human Agreement", "quote": "Qwen3-Max--A & 90.7 / .820 & 91.3 / .827", "why": "judge-사람 일치 수치"}
{"id": "e212", "source": "p1", "locator": "부록 Judge--Human Agreement", "quote": "A--B & 82.0 / .687 & 92.7 / .853", "why": "사람-사람 일치"}
{"id": "e213", "source": "p2", "locator": "§1 Introduction", "quote": "In an early prototype of ours, the optimizer improved the judge by deleting it.", "why": "judge 를 지운 최적화"}
{"id": "e214", "source": "p2", "locator": "§1 Introduction", "quote": "The second is \\emph{deterministic gating}: the checks with final authority are mechanical rules, and a mechanical rejection overrides an LLM approval, never the reverse.", "why": "결정적 gate 가 우선"}
{"id": "e215", "source": "p2", "locator": "§2.1 Roles", "quote": "Receives the current prompt and the failing training cases with their verdicts, and returns a root-cause diagnosis. It is explicitly forbidden from proposing prompt text.", "why": "진단과 작성의 분리"}
{"id": "e216", "source": "p2", "locator": "§2.1 Roles", "quote": "Separating diagnosis from authorship prevents the common failure in which a single model invents an explanation that conveniently justifies the edit it already wanted to make.", "why": "분리의 이유"}
{"id": "e217", "source": "p2", "locator": "§2.3 Why role decoupling", "quote": "No component both proposes and applies. No component both judges and acts.", "why": "역할 분리"}
{"id": "e218", "source": "p2", "locator": "§3 Class C", "quote": "An upstream pipeline that converted human feedback into golden labels keyed on the presence of a specific string in metadata; when absent, it defaulted the label to \\emph{non-violative}, even where the annotator's free-text comment explicitly described the clause as violative.", "why": "정답 label 이 뒤집힌 원인"}
{"id": "e219", "source": "p2", "locator": "§4.1 Amplification", "quote": "its mutation \\textbf{stripped the tax-compliance rules out of the target prompt} to maximize agreement with the corrupted judge", "why": "틀린 정답에 맞춰 규칙을 지웠다"}
{"id": "e220", "source": "p2", "locator": "§4.1 Amplification", "quote": "The loop converted a data bug into a capability regression: the optimized agent was measurably better by the metric and objectively worse at the task.", "why": "지표는 좋아지고 일은 나빠졌다"}
{"id": "e221", "source": "p2", "locator": "§3 Class D", "quote": "Measured reasoning-alignment pass rate jumped from 23.1\\% to 80.0\\%. The agent's actual precision in identifying defects did not change at all", "why": "judge 어휘에 맞춘 상승"}
{"id": "e222", "source": "p2", "locator": "§5.7 Limits", "quote": "Of the thirteen automated rejections and reversions logged across our runs, six were metric-regression reversions: mutations that passed the mechanical pre-apply checks, were approved by the Teacher, and then measurably degraded performance when evaluated, in one case dropping a suite from 88.9\\% to 33.3\\%.", "why": "LLM 승인 후 회귀"}
{"id": "e223", "source": "p2", "locator": "§5.7 Limits", "quote": "Retry loops risk reproducing the convergence dynamic we criticize.", "why": "재시도가 judge 에 수렴"}
{"id": "e224", "source": "p2", "locator": "§5.5 L5", "quote": "We plant intentionally unpassable cases inside evaluation suites, cases whose reference answer cannot be produced by honest analysis.", "why": "canary 사례"}
{"id": "e225", "source": "p2", "locator": "§Limitations", "quote": "Single-run measurements.", "why": "저자 한계: 단일 실행"}
{"id": "e226", "source": "p2", "locator": "§Limitations", "quote": "The systems described here run on internal infrastructure that cannot be released, so this work is not directly reproducible.", "why": "재현 불가"}
{"id": "e227", "source": "p2", "locator": "§2.5 Ground truth", "quote": "Nine of the ten are legal and commercial document review, which is where the bulk of our production use sits", "why": "도메인: 법무, 상업 문서 검토"}
{"id": "e228", "source": "p3", "locator": "§3.2 Rule adaptation", "quote": "A \\emph{Reversal} stream changes the relation that the agent learned during its first three updates.", "why": "규칙 반전 시험"}
{"id": "e229", "source": "p3", "locator": "§4.2 Rule adaptation", "quote": "acquiring useful rules does not ensure their correction upon encountering contradictory evidence. Notably, no revision effect remains statistically significant after Holm correction.", "why": "규칙 수정은 유의하지 않다"}
{"id": "e230", "source": "p3", "locator": "§4.4 acceptance rule", "quote": "Overall, safeguards provide greater stability mainly by accepting fewer updates, rather than by identifying better candidates.", "why": "gate 는 덜 받아들여서 안정적"}
{"id": "e231", "source": "p3", "locator": "§4.5 Forgetting", "quote": "SkillBoost achieves the highest positive BWT, yet performance still declines on $21.3\\%$ of trajectories.", "why": "망각은 꼬리에 몰린다"}
{"id": "e232", "source": "p3", "locator": "§Conclusion", "quote": "current acceptance rules have limited capacity to distinguish transferable improvements from overfitting, or necessary rule revision from harmful forgetting", "why": "수용 규칙이 의도된 수정과 망각을 못 가른다"}
{"id": "e233", "source": "p4", "locator": "§Introduction", "quote": "to recommend the correct remediation---CREATE (content missing) vs.\\ UPDATE (content exists but wrong)---the agent must verify whether the content actually exists.", "why": "공백과 낡음 구분"}
{"id": "e234", "source": "p4", "locator": "§Ablation 2", "quote": "Full Exploration & 96\\% & 83\\% & 67\\%", "why": "탐색 있음"}
{"id": "e235", "source": "p4", "locator": "§Ablation 2", "quote": "Passive (no exploration) & 90\\% & 33\\% & 62\\%", "why": "탐색 없음"}
{"id": "e236", "source": "p4", "locator": "§Component Type Accuracy", "quote": "Skills and prompts achieve perfect attribution; KB and tools are harder due to ambiguous file boundaries.", "why": "층별 귀속 정확도"}
{"id": "e237", "source": "p4", "locator": "§Why Synthetic Data", "quote": "Confidentiality requirements preclude disclosure of real interaction data, context sources, or system architecture details.", "why": "합성 데이터로 평가한 이유"}
{"id": "e238", "source": "p4", "locator": "§Architecture Component Overview", "quote": "Outputs a \\texttt{CRUD\\-Recommendation} for human review.", "why": "사람 검토로 끝난다"}
{"id": "e239", "source": "p4", "locator": "§Ablation 2", "quote": "Exploration ablation on 60 traces.", "why": "표본 60"}
{"id": "e240", "source": "p5", "locator": "§Post-Task Memory Curation", "quote": "It is the only agent allowed to mutate\n\\(\\mathcal{M}\\).", "why": "curator 만 메모리를 바꾼다"}
{"id": "e241", "source": "p5", "locator": "§Environment-Probing Curation", "quote": "a third retains the removed\n\\texttt{attrs\\_g3} name after schema drift", "why": "궤적만 보면 낡은 사실이 남는다"}
{"id": "e242", "source": "p5", "locator": "§Environment-Probing Curation", "quote": "After\nproposing a candidate memory, it makes targeted read-only tool calls to\ninvestigate specific uncertainties, then uses the observations to create,\nrevise, narrow, delete, or skip the record.", "why": "propose-probe-commit"}
{"id": "e243", "source": "p5", "locator": "§Abstract", "quote": "On CLBench, probing raises pass rate from 39\\%\nto 73\\%", "why": "probing 효과"}
{"id": "e244", "source": "p6", "locator": "§Results: Knowledge access", "quote": "Given only the question, a plain BM25 search over the same\ncached records answers 15--17. \\mimeo{} leads by three to five questions and\nloses none, but exact paired tests do not separate them.", "why": "증류 파일 대 BM25"}
{"id": "e245", "source": "p6", "locator": "§Results: Knowledge access", "quote": "It does not yet establish a benefit\nfrom distillation.", "why": "증류 이득 미확인"}
{"id": "e246", "source": "p6", "locator": "§Results: Judgment transfer", "quote": "E6 therefore gives no\nevidence either for or against judgment transfer.", "why": "판단 이전 미확인"}
{"id": "e247", "source": "p7", "locator": "§Introduction", "quote": "Under the default order, the agent using ReasoningBank achieves an average performance gain of 1.5\\%; however, when evaluated under randomly shuffled task orders, the agent exhibits a performance degradation of 4.5\\%.", "why": "과제 순서 의존"}
{"id": "e248", "source": "p7", "locator": "§3.3 Task Order", "quote": "The default task order in prior works imposes an implicit, easy-to-hard curriculum", "why": "암묵적 커리큘럼"}
{"id": "e249", "source": "p8", "locator": "§Agreement, different conditions, and conflicts", "quote": "An unresolved contradiction remains visible as linked alternatives for review or adjudication. It should not become an unconditionally active rule.", "why": "미해결 모순은 비활성"}
{"id": "e250", "source": "p8", "locator": "§Agreement, different conditions, and conflicts", "quote": "A requirement grounded in a standard or procedure cannot be settled by a simple vote or a compromise with preferences.", "why": "표결로 정하지 않는다"}
{"id": "e251", "source": "p8", "locator": "§Agreement, different conditions, and conflicts", "quote": "If the overlap is empty, both rules can be retained within the checked task scope.", "why": "범위가 겹치지 않으면 둘 다 유지"}
{"id": "e252", "source": "p8", "locator": "§Cross-review and version management", "quote": "Each update creates a new version. Dependencies identify skills that need revalidation after a rule changes.", "why": "규칙 변경 후 재검증 대상"}
{"id": "e253", "source": "p8", "locator": "§Cross-review and version management", "quote": "Human confirmation is recorded separately: 9 candidates had completed human verification and 331 were marked as awaiting it.", "why": "사람 확인 병목"}
{"id": "e254", "source": "p8", "locator": "§Abstract", "quote": "Under common task inputs and scoring criteria, the base model, raw-corpus retrieval-augmented generation (RAG), and \\product agent scored 70.63, 79.75, and 89.58, respectively.", "why": "원자료 RAG 대비"}
{"id": "e255", "source": "p8", "locator": "§Agreement, different conditions, and conflicts", "quote": "When different conditions explain different recommendations, both procedures remain available with explicit conditions.", "why": "조건이 다르면 둘 다"}
{"id": "e256", "source": "w3", "locator": "§The core idea", "quote": "noting where new data contradicts old claims, strengthening or challenging the evolving synthesis", "why": "ingest 때 모순 표시"}
{"id": "e257", "source": "c1", "locator": "§1.1 Combined update policies", "quote": "In this exploratory sweep, Accept Every Edit is associated\nwith a higher average oracle diagnostic for gpt-5.5 on all three\nbenchmarks.", "why": "gate 없는 정책이 강한 모델에서 더 높았다: SkillOpt 를 같은 방향 근거에서 뺀 이유"}
{"id": "e258", "source": "c1", "locator": "§1.1 Combined update policies", "quote": "The comparison changes both the candidate gate and the\nslow-update policy, so it cannot identify the effect of either mechanism by\nitself.", "why": "저자 단서"}
{"id": "e259", "source": "p8", "locator": "§Experimental setup, Scoring and run records", "quote": "An LLM applies a shared rubric to score A, B, and C on the same questions across seven dimensions", "why": "점수는 LLM 이 rubric 으로 매겼다"}
{"id": "e260", "source": "p8", "locator": "§Experimental setup, Sample processing", "quote": "This report uses a random sample of 20 authorized users. Their 1,576 source files yield 30,762 retrievable chunks", "why": "표본 20명, 원자료 1,576개"}
